Subject: [PATCH] let a GART-bound queue reach memory outside the aperture

Second defect introduced by aac939813f, same shape as the first: a permissive
path in Gfx12GartTranslator::translate() replaced by a hard reject. The older
577edec042 line of development passed an out-of-aperture address through as a
direct VmMemoryDomain::Local access; this head faults it.

That breaks the driver's own SDMA page table update. The page tables live in
VRAM -- on this device the PTE store targets 0x68ec000, beside the page
directory root at 0x6900000 and far outside the aperture at
[0x6c00000000, 0x6c1fffffff]. Measured on an instrumented build:

  vm: access fault at 0x68ec000 (base 0x68ec000 +0) size=4096 kind=1 outcome=2
  sdma: latching faulted at cursor 0x1a8 ring=[0x6c00209000+0x2000] fetched=24
    words=[0x00000004 0x00223000 0x0000006c 0x00000008 0x00000000 0x00000000]

Read that packet with the model's own decoder: word 0 is opcode 4, kOpIndirect,
and join(word1, word2) puts the indirect buffer at 0x6c00223000 -- inside the
aperture, so the IB fetch itself succeeds. kind=1 is VmAccessKind::Write and
outcome=2 is VmAccessOutcome::Faulted, so what actually fails is the 4096-byte
PTE write to 0x68ec000 that the IB carries; the IB is merely the frame that
latches the fault. The fence never signals and the guest hangs in
kfd_ioctl_acquire_vm with "ring sdma0.0 timeout, signaled seq=2, emitted
seq=3". A control image built from 909c17f runs the same guest with zero SDMA
timeouts.

Note for review: the GART walk's own PTE reads are NOT affected by this check.
Gfx12GartTranslator reads its entry via memory_->read(VmMemoryDomain::Local,
...) directly, below translation, so the aperture check never sees them. Only
driver-issued traffic routed through GpuVmAccess is affected.

Restore the pass-through, keeping the head's in-aperture body unchanged.

Two limitations this inherits from the pass-through it restores, both worth
fixing separately rather than silently: the aperture_start_ != 0 sentinel means
a GART legitimately published with aperture_start == 0 disables translation for
the whole space, and the pass-through grants Mtype::RW with full RWX to any
64-bit address with no bound against local memory size.

diff --git a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
index 77c5adc5d8..180358fda6 100644
--- a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
+++ b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
@@ -526,8 +537,35 @@ VmTranslationResult Gfx12GartTranslator::translate(uint64_t address, std::size_t
   if (size == 0 || size - 1 > std::numeric_limits<uint64_t>::max() - address)
     return {.outcome = VmAccessOutcome::Malformed, .translation = {}};
 
-  if (address < aperture_start_ || address > aperture_end_)
-    return {.outcome = VmAccessOutcome::Faulted, .translation = {}};
+  // A GART-bound queue does not only touch the GART. The driver's own SDMA page
+  // table update carries a write to the page tables themselves, which live in
+  // VRAM: on this device the PTE store targets 0x68ec000, beside the page
+  // directory root at 0x6900000 and far outside the aperture at
+  // [0x6c00000000, 0x6c1fffffff]. Faulting everything outside the aperture kills
+  // that update -- the write returns Faulted, the indirect buffer carrying it
+  // latches the fault, the fence never signals, and the guest hangs in
+  // kfd_ioctl_acquire_vm with "ring sdma0.0 timeout, signaled seq=2, emitted
+  // seq=3". Pass an out-of-aperture address through as a direct local access,
+  // clamping the reported run so a range starting below the aperture cannot
+  // claim to cover into it.
+  const bool in_aperture =
+      aperture_start_ != 0 && address >= aperture_start_ && address <= aperture_end_;
+  if (!in_aperture) {
+    uint64_t contiguous_bytes = size;
+    if (aperture_start_ != 0 && address < aperture_start_)
+      contiguous_bytes = std::min<uint64_t>(contiguous_bytes, aperture_start_ - address);
+    return {
+        .outcome = VmAccessOutcome::Complete,
+        .translation =
+            {
+                .domain = VmMemoryDomain::Local,
+                .address = address,
+                .contiguous_bytes = contiguous_bytes,
+                .mtype = Mtype::RW,
+                .permissions = {.readable = true, .writable = true, .executable = true},
+            },
+    };
+  }
 
   const uint64_t pte_address_mask = gfx12_pte_address_mask(config_);
   const uint64_t table = page_table_base_ & pte_address_mask;
